<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Restoration Shaman Healer in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from dungeons, reputations, and professions. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c7">Best in Slot Gear for Restoration Shaman Healer in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Restoration Shamans see a few major changes to itemization in Cataclysm: all HoTs can now crit, and Mp5 is no longer a stat, as it was replaced by Spirit, which now provides good benefits to all healers and not just <a class="icontiny c5" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=5/priest">
<img alt="Priest" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_priest.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Priest</span></a>s and <a class="icontiny c11" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=11/druid">
<img alt="Druid" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Druid</span></a>s. Most importantly, Cataclysm brings armor specialization - which means that wearing all mail grants us 5% extra Intellect through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86529/mail-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mail Specialization</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Overall, our primary gearing goals will be to stack Spirit for extra regen for ourselves and the raid with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16190/mana-tide-totem">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_summonwaterelemental.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mana Tide Totem</span></a>, and get enough Haste to hit a breakpoint on one of your heal over time effects. Afterwards, Mastery and Crit both have their upsides and downsides, with Mastery being at its best on hard fights that take allies to the brink of death, making it better for progression raiding.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intellect - This stat now gives Spell Power by itself, on top of the Mana and Crit that it provided in WotLK. We now gem Intellect, which is a red gem now, just like SP was.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit - Our core regeneration stat and main way to scale <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16190/mana-tide-totem">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_summonwaterelemental.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mana Tide Totem</span></a>. The 5 second rule is completely gone in Cataclysm, there's only "in combat" and "out of combat" regen.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Haste now always affects all of our HoTs, including <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=73920/healing-rain">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_giftofthewaterspirit.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Healing Rain</span></a>, where the benefit is felt at specific breakpoints where you gain extra ticks. Haste between breakpoints is still good for faster casting of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=1064/chain-heal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_healingwavegreater.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chain Heal</span></a> and single-target heals regardless, as well as faster <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=403/lightning-bolt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_lightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Bolt</span></a>s for <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82988/telluric-currents">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_lightning_lightningbolt01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Telluric Currents</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - This is a new stat that buffs all of our healing proportionally to the healing missing from the target. You can gain quite a lot of extra healing from it if you are frequently healing deeply injured targets, making it a great stat when it matters the most.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - All of our HoTs can now crit and critical healing does 200% healing in Cataclysm, up from 150% in previous expansions. Restoration also has multiple talent effects that only work after a critical strike such as <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16235/ancestral-healing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_undyingstrength.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ancestral Healing</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=51558/ancestral-awakening">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_ancestralawakening.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ancestral Awakening</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=16196/resurgence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_shaman_watershield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Resurgence</span></a>, making it a good stat even with its poor rating to 1% crit conversion ratio.</div></li></ol>
